{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap","id":762480,"title":"Idea for the Pure in 2e (stop gap)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-10T12:01:43-08:00","id":762480,"title":"Idea for the Pure in 2e (stop gap)","content":"So, I was reading over The Pure as my players have stated that they're interested in dealing with a Pure Pack in or near their territory and I was thinking that I might update the Anguish, Disease, Fervor, Savagery and Scourging gifts. What I found was that Anguish and Disease can VERY easily be updated to 2nd edition rules as Shadow gifts that just aren't common among the forsaken (though I do know a spirit in Green Lawn that can definitely teach Anguish) while Fervor, Savagery and Scourging feel almost like Moon Gifts.<br /> <br /> So that got me thinking. Since the Pure purge their Moon Gifts along with their auspices and have no &quot;Ghost Wolf&quot; equivalent and receive Purity as an automatic Renown, just like the Forsaken receive Auspice Renown, what if they also receive a Totem Gift? Gifts unique to their totem that they receive based on their Purity (their connection to their dedication to their totem's ideal) yes I know that each of these tribes receives a different Renown (Wisdom, Honor and Glory respectively) but I see those based upon their Tribe's purpose more than Ideal.<br /> <br /> Also, as all werewolves receive a free dot of Totem, I'm going to go and assume that the Pure begin play with 2 dots of Totem (because Dude, Yes!) meaning that we're looking at a pack with a totem touching 4 - 5 dots of rank. RUN.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> things I've missed?<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:24:26-08:00","id":762500,"title":"","content":"Why wouldn't Forsaken have totem gifts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:37:21-08:00","id":762514,"title":"","content":"Because they're totems expect them to do things on their own, they're given autonomy and banes that allow them to live their lives, albeit through a particular lens. The Pure tribal totems are eldritch totalitarians who foist upon their children harsh and all consuming banes that force them to live their lives away from the world and keep them tightly under their thumb. I see the Tribal gift as a side-effect rather of that control.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T12:57:41-08:00","id":762530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gnomish American</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap#post762480\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I was reading over The Pure as my players have stated that they're interested in dealing with a Pure Pack in or near their territory and I was thinking that I might update the Anguish, Disease, Fervor, Savagery and Scourging gifts. What I found was that Anguish and Disease can VERY easily be updated to 2nd edition rules as Shadow gifts that just aren't common among the forsaken (though I do know a spirit in Green Lawn that can definitely teach Anguish) while Fervor, Savagery and Scourging feel almost like Moon Gifts.<br /> <br /> So that got me thinking. Since the Pure purge their Moon Gifts along with their auspices and have no &quot;Ghost Wolf&quot; equivalent and receive Purity as an automatic Renown, just like the Forsaken receive Auspice Renown, what if they also receive a Totem Gift? Gifts unique to their totem that they receive based on their Purity (their connection to their dedication to their totem's ideal) yes I know that each of these tribes receives a different Renown (Wisdom, Honor and Glory respectively) but I see those based upon their Tribe's purpose more than Ideal.<br /> <br /> Also, as all werewolves receive a free dot of Totem, I'm going to go and assume that the Pure begin play with 2 dots of Totem (because Dude, Yes!) meaning that we're looking at a pack with a totem touching 4 - 5 dots of rank. RUN.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?<br /> <br /> things I've missed?<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> I assume you mean Agony rather than Anguish?<br /> <br /> Anyway, Pure get an extra Shadow Gift and a bonus dot of Totem in place of their Auspice stuff.<br /> <br /> I'd not be keen on unique Totem Gifts, as part of my larger antipathy to any form of restricted Shadow Gift. If it exists as a Shadow Gift - ie anything that is not Moon or Wolf - any Uratha can get it. Don't expect Lodge-unique Gifts, for example.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:00:33-08:00","id":762534,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I saw you post something similar on another thread, and that makes sense, It just means that I have to do even more work while doing my house rules (those particular gifts lists don't follow the 1 gift per Renown rule) ah well, c'est la vie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:00:57-08:00","id":762537,"title":"","content":"Keep in mind that the new design on Gifts assume that there's no monopoly from any specific group on shadow gifts. A given tribe/auspice only has an easier time unlocking certain gifts because the spirits associated with them teach them more readily, not because there's some ban that prevents them to teach them to another, should they be subjected to the Siskur Dah, for example.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-10T13:02:39-08:00","id":762540,"title":"","content":"I know, When I said &quot;tribal&quot; gift I mean a tiered gift like a moon gift, that automatically raised with their purity. Even in 1e I played it so that any Uratha could take any gift so long as they found a spirit to teach them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Call Me <b>Ray</b>.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://southern-gothic.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Southern Gothic </a>- Welcome to New Calais","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/256-gnomish-american","name":"Gnomish American","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar256_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"569"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T00:19:22-08:00","id":762887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=762530#post762530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, Pure get an extra Shadow Gift and a bonus dot of Totem in place of their Auspice stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, with that each werewolf adds minimum 2 Totem points and Pure packs ar much numbered to the typical Forsaken packs - like 6-10 Pure in compare to 3-5 Forsaken - it quickly would mean that Pure Totem grants them twice the normal power!<br /> <br /> No wonder that Pure are turning away from the unstable Moon and Lunes. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=762530#post762530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd not be keen on unique Totem Gifts, as part of my larger antipathy to any form of restricted Shadow Gift. If it exists as a Shadow Gift - ie anything that is not Moon or Wolf - any Uratha can get it. Don't expect Lodge-unique Gifts, for example.</div> </div> </div> </div>But I assume Lodges still makes some Gifts &quot;affinites&quot;? Like all Uratha can learn Gift of Disease, but the <i>Lodge of Sickness</i> can learn it just like Auspice or Tribe, yes?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T00:25:44-08:00","id":762888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=762887#post762887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">[I]t quickly would mean that Pure Totem grants them twice the normal power!<br /> <br /> No wonder that Pure are turning away from the unstable Moon and Lunes.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wyrd, take a look at the Totem rules again.<br /> <br /> Notice that the chart tops out on distributed benefits for the pack.<br /> <br /> Now notice that there <i>is</i> no effective ceiling on benefits for the totem itself to derive from Totem points.<br /> <br /> Now remember what the Pure's totems were like in 1e.<br /> <br /> Now remember how pack bans work in 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T05:58:36-08:00","id":763036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=762887#post762887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But I assume Lodges still makes some Gifts &quot;affinites&quot;? Like all Uratha can learn Gift of Disease, but the <i>Lodge of Sickness</i> can learn it just like Auspice or Tribe, yes?</div> </div> </div> </div> Nope, that's not a think that Lodges do. Lodge bonds are different.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T06:02:27-08:00","id":763040,"title":"","content":"Just to expand on that a bit: Lodges giving XP discounts/affinities/whatnot were barse-ackwards in terms of incentives.<br /> <br /> If a theoretical Lodge of Sickness gave a discount on the Gift of Disease, then paradoxically Uratha PCs wanting to join that Lodge were always worse off if they actually bought it before joining the Lodge. In other words, Uratha going down the thematic line of being good at Thing X were in a worse situation when joining the Lodge Focused On Thing X than a character who had specifically not spent any XP on it. This applied to Gift affinities, skill XP discounts, etc etc.<br /> <br /> New Lodge bonds never give XP discounts. You get quite a lot out of being in a Lodge, but it's all... other stuff. Not discounts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T06:14:44-08:00","id":763049,"title":"","content":"You tease way too much, Chris.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T06:45:39-08:00","id":763067,"title":"","content":"I try my best!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:14:22-08:00","id":763078,"title":"","content":"Perhaps this thread of mine might help? I already do have a write-up of the Agony and Savagery Gifts as 2e, but struggling with the rest.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/filedata/fetch?filedataid=1074\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion\"> Werewolf Gifts - 2e Conversion - Onyx Path Forums </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion\"> http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/740377-werewolf-gifts-2e-conversion </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> Seeing as Werewolf 2e players have a shortage of official Moon Gifts as well as Gifts tied to the Pure, I'm putting up this thread for those interested in </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:20:24-08:00","id":763082,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem you both might be having is trying to translate the gifts so closely to their original form. Certainly some of the first edition gifts translated over but for the most part we have entirely new facets. You aren't limited by the increasing 'power level' offered by the first edition gift structure.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:28:58-08:00","id":763091,"title":"","content":"Indeed. Were I to rewrite the Pure Gifts into 2e I would:<br /> <br /> a) argue for dumping Scourging entirely and replacing it with something else.<br /> b) bin most of the existing Gifts in the lists.<br /> c) insist Fervour be made about general religious fervour rather than Gurim: the Rabid Wolfening.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T07:57:57-08:00","id":763109,"title":"","content":"Chris, the freelancer we deserve, not the one we need.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T15:34:35-08:00","id":763526,"title":"","content":"When you say an extra Shadow Gift, do you mean that they <i>unlock</i> an extra Shadow Gift at character creation? Or do they get an extra Facet?<br /> <br /> I'm also assuming that their starting Renown dots look like a Ghost Wolf's, since they lack the dot from Auspice. Do all Pure still have Purity as their Tribal Renown?<br /> <br /> Hmm...<br /> <br /> <b>Ivory Claws:</b> Honor and Purity<br /> <b>Predator Kings:</b> Glory and Purity<br /> <b>Fire-Touched:</b> Either Cunning and Purity or Purity and Wisdom; not sure which fits better.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T15:38:43-08:00","id":763531,"title":"","content":"I presume he means they get an extra unlocked shadow gift, so the number of starting gifts is the same as for a forsaken. So three shadow facets and a wolf facet, presumably.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T17:38:30-08:00","id":763611,"title":"","content":"I guess that would depend on whether Pure shares a similar method of character creation and they want to balance them against one another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-11T22:44:58-08:00","id":763791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763526#post763526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When you say an extra Shadow Gift, do you mean that they <i>unlock</i> an extra Shadow Gift at character creation? Or do they get an extra Facet?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes (and yes, by default)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763526#post763526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also assuming that their starting Renown dots look like a Ghost Wolf's, since they lack the dot from Auspice. Do all Pure still have Purity as their Tribal Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, and no.<br /> <br /> Soon...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T00:50:43-08:00","id":763845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763791#post763791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes (and yes, by default)<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> No, and no.<br /> <br /> Soon...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh god, the hunger for spoilers is starting to burn again. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T13:54:45-08:00","id":764366,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763791#post763791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, and no.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not clear. In 1e, the Purity Renown is granted in lieu of Auspice Renown, and independent of Tribe (Claws got Honor, Touched got Wisdom, and Kings got Glory). Is it no longer the case that Pure get that eponymous Renown? Because, eponymous. Or was the second &quot;no&quot; meant as a corrective to the idea that Purity was Tribal?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T16:43:23-08:00","id":764512,"title":"","content":"The thing is that all renown purchases are 3xp. And there's no artificial speedbumps in the form of &quot;You better raise your auspice or tribal renown to 3 if you want Glory 3.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T20:54:52-08:00","id":764696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=764366#post764366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not clear. In 1e, the Purity Renown is granted in lieu of Auspice Renown, and independent of Tribe (Claws got Honor, Touched got Wisdom, and Kings got Glory). Is it no longer the case that Pure get that eponymous Renown? Because, eponymous. Or was the second &amp;quot;no&amp;quot; meant as a corrective to the idea that Purity was Tribal?</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763526#post763526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also assuming that their starting Renown dots look like a Ghost Wolf's, since they lack the dot from Auspice.</div> </div> </div> </div>No,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>amechra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763526#post763526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Do all Pure still have Purity as their Tribal Renown?</div> </div> </div> </div>and no.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T21:49:51-08:00","id":764721,"title":"","content":"Ok, it was just a question, meant in good faith. If I posed it rudely, I apologize.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-12T22:50:02-08:00","id":764735,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verge</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=764721#post764721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ok, it was just a question, meant in good faith. If I posed it rudely, I apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>Apologies for any terseness, trying to clarify on phone with shitty auto correct and clumsy thumbs.<br /> <br /> Edit: Right, better keyboard now. <br /> <br /> Part 1 - Pure Renown distribution is different to Ghost Wolves. <br /> <br /> Part 2 - The Renown of Pure is more involved than all of them simply having Purity as tribal Renown.<br /> <br /> In both cases, I can't yet share exactly how they work, but it hopefully won't be too much longer before further details come to light. (And Chris has a lot of great ideas around the Pure, and indeed all things Werewolf.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 11-13-2015, 04:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T05:33:38-08:00","id":764877,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=763091#post763091\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Indeed. Were I to rewrite the Pure Gifts into 2e I would:<br /> <br /> a) argue for dumping Scourging entirely and replacing it with something else.<br /> b) bin most of the existing Gifts in the lists.<br /> c) insist Fervour be made about general religious fervour rather than Gurim: the Rabid Wolfening.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div> To give a sorta example on this, were I looking at, say, the Agony Gift list, my current thoughts would be:<br /> - Stoicism: Cut it or heavily rework. An Uratha can end up with no wound penalties off 3 dots of Iron Stamina, so for such a character this would literally do nothing, and it would mean that the associated Renown would cap out in effect at 3 dots.<br /> - Barbed Arrow: Core idea of applying a pain-based debilitating effect isn't bad. Rework but keep in an altered form.<br /> - Pangs of Anguish: 'Killing you' gift that deals damage straight-up. Cut.<br /> - World of Pain: Too narrow in concept and target, plus applying debilitating effects would already be present in the reworked evolution of Barbed Arrow. Cut.<br /> - All-Consuming Excruciation: 'This hurts so bad that it's REALLY gonna screw you up' probably applies as a high-end effect on the reworked Barbed Arrow already. Cut, but parts of this might be salvageable for a new and different Facet.<br /> <br /> In general, expect 2e Gifts to be heavily altered, refined and focused over 1e lists.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T11:12:07-08:00","id":765054,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=764735#post764735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies for any terseness, trying to clarify on phone with shitty auto correct and clumsy thumbs.<br /> In both cases, I can't yet share exactly how they work, but it hopefully won't be too much longer before further details come to light. (And Chris has a lot of great ideas around the Pure, and indeed all things Werewolf.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the clarification, and I'm sorry I went &quot;sorry to affront&quot; on you, I just didn't see an option for moving the conversation forward without swerving into more dickish realms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T22:30:45-08:00","id":765357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=764877#post764877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To give a sorta example on this, were I looking at, say, the Agony Gift list, my current thoughts would be:<br /> - Stoicism: Cut it or heavily rework. An Uratha can end up with no wound penalties off 3 dots of Iron Stamina, so for such a character this would literally do nothing, and it would mean that the associated Renown would cap out in effect at 3 dots.<br /> - Barbed Arrow: Core idea of applying a pain-based debilitating effect isn't bad. Rework but keep in an altered form.<br /> - Pangs of Anguish: 'Killing you' gift that deals damage straight-up. Cut.<br /> - World of Pain: Too narrow in concept and target, plus applying debilitating effects would already be present in the reworked evolution of Barbed Arrow. Cut.<br /> - All-Consuming Excruciation: 'This hurts so bad that it's REALLY gonna screw you up' probably applies as a high-end effect on the reworked Barbed Arrow already. Cut, but parts of this might be salvageable for a new and different Facet.<br /> <br /> In general, expect 2e Gifts to be heavily altered, refined and focused over 1e lists.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I just want to say that I love what you(and everyone else who writes for this) are doing with gifts in 2e. Its one of the highlights of the game for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-13T23:19:23-08:00","id":765378,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/762480-idea-for-the-pure-in-2e-stop-gap?p=764877#post764877\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To give a sorta example on this, were I looking at, say, the Agony Gift list, my current thoughts would be:<br /> - Stoicism: Cut it or heavily rework. An Uratha can end up with no wound penalties off 3 dots of Iron Stamina, so for such a character this would literally do nothing, and it would mean that the associated Renown would cap out in effect at 3 dots.<br /> - Barbed Arrow: Core idea of applying a pain-based debilitating effect isn't bad. Rework but keep in an altered form.<br /> - Pangs of Anguish: 'Killing you' gift that deals damage straight-up. Cut.<br /> - World of Pain: Too narrow in concept and target, plus applying debilitating effects would already be present in the reworked evolution of Barbed Arrow. Cut.<br /> - All-Consuming Excruciation: 'This hurts so bad that it's REALLY gonna screw you up' probably applies as a high-end effect on the reworked Barbed Arrow already. Cut, but parts of this might be salvageable for a new and different Facet.<br /> <br /> In general, expect 2e Gifts to be heavily altered, refined and focused over 1e lists.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm definitely noting this for the next time I revise the Agony Gift.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8180-deionscribe","name":"Deionscribe","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2265"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-14T04:46:22-08:00","id":765481,"title":"","content":"Of course, I forgot to mention the key things to keep in mind - Gifts need to reflect the Urathas' nature, not just be a grab-bag of random powers with little thematic linking to werewolves/hunters/shamans. Designing a Gift under 2e requires looking at it from those points of view as well, which adds to the level of reworking involved in translating 1e Gift lists over.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T19:05:50-08:00","id":766744,"title":"","content":"I've been a huge fan of WtF 2E's...texture. Everything feels like snapping maws and spurting blood and mouths full of throbbing flesh and fur, and the Gifts really seem like they belong, more than they did in 1E or even Apocalypse.<br /> <br /> I'd love more information on how the Urdaga and Anshega experience their Gifts in a cultural lens, particularly why one Tribe might lay claim to a Gift that is also the purview of an Auspice. Surely each division is aware of their strengths, but does an Ithaeur Blood Talon watching a Storm Lord wielding Elemental Influence think? Does the first recognize the mark of the Gift in the second's spirit? Does she question the deeds that earned him that Facet? Would she recognize the same sensations when he describes its use to her? And when they wrestle a Predator King's will for control over an inferno, do they see only a misguided rival, or do they see a perversion?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-15T19:21:05-08:00","id":766753,"title":"","content":"I think you'd have to be a real purist to get bothered by something like that. Like, it's probably an adequate response for the Pure. But since the gifts are carved on a werewolf, Forsaken probably don't really need to question the deeds done in exchange for them.<br /> <br /> Since gifts are 'unlocked' so to speak werewolves probably appreciate not everyone in their tribe or auspice is going to have the same gifts available to them. My own character has recently, finally, broken into the Death gifts. And while some other elodoth or Iron Masters would probably be surprised it doesn't seem like it would be a point of contention more than one of curiosity.<br /> <br /> Personally I'd have Forsaken view a Pure with similar abilities as more of a rival, especially as the similarities stacked up. And I'd probably run a more similar outlook from the Pure, except tainted with the kind of disdain that leads to them trying to convert the Uratha rather than simply kill them. 'He could be so much better, he could be like me, if only he threw off the shackles of the Bitch Goddess.' Or something similar.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't rule out some sort of hate-on, though, I just think it would be rare and mostly based around rare or specialized spirits. Like Tony Markov from Night Horrors and his ergot-spirit allies or certain lodges.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-15-2015, 10:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T12:19:41-08:00","id":768001,"title":"","content":"I'm simply more curious about the emotional and cultural connections werewolves have to their Gifts and Facets, since that sort of thing has come out more in the new edition, and not so much the social ramifications. Tribe, et al, are useful lenses for looking at that connection. If a Storm Lord were to learn a Facet of Agony, she might see it as a learning tool, where an Ivory Claw sees the same as a communion with Silver Wolf, and would regard the Talon as a blasphemer. The former might have suffered a lot to learn the Facet, but saw it as a trial to overcome, and now pushes down the pain. The latter feels the pain is sacred, and lets it wash over himself as well as his enemies. The Talon inflicts the sensation of tearing flesh and breaking bones, while the Claw nauseates and fevers the foe. It's that sort of ripe territory I would like to seem exploration of, as Gifts have moved from spell-like phenomena to integral, spiritual awakenings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>LFP: Foreign Bodies (Deviant: the Renegades)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/969-verge","name":"Verge","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-17T12:28:40-08:00","id":768010,"title":"","content":"The thing is while gifts and facets have opened up, so to have the points of view of werewolves. There isn't an auspice or tribe, Forsaken or not, that is a hive mind.<br /> <br /> This is more the kind of thing to explore in your own games, as well as the reactions to it, than seek all-encompassing answers for in the books. At least an answer beyond, 'It depends.' So far, rules as written, one Ivory Claw in your game may feel that way, an entire pack might, or even the entire tribe might in your own setting, if you want to do that. If not, you're free to have them not care.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 11-17-2015, 03:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}